<div>
<p begin="00:00:00.160" end="00:00:05.520" style="s2">Thank you very much everybody.</p>
<p begin="00:00:02.800" end="00:00:08.240" style="s2">Wow.</p>
<p begin="00:00:05.520" end="00:00:11.679" style="s2">You should have seen you should have</p>
<p begin="00:00:08.240" end="00:00:13.599" style="s2">seen the ride in from the airport. Every</p>
<p begin="00:00:11.679" end="00:00:17.480" style="s2">block, every inch, every everything.</p>
<p begin="00:00:13.599" end="00:00:17.480" style="s2">There&#39;s so many people.</p>
<p begin="00:00:18.560" end="00:00:25.199" style="s2">Thousands and thousands and Hello, Ohio.</p>
<p begin="00:00:22.960" end="00:00:29.000" style="s2">You know,</p>
<p begin="00:00:25.199" end="00:00:29.000" style="s2">I love this house.</p>
<p begin="00:00:29.279" end="00:00:34.000" style="s2">People don&#39;t know I worked in Ohio for a</p>
<p begin="00:00:31.920" end="00:00:39.360" style="s2">big beautiful summer when I was a young</p>
<p begin="00:00:34.000" end="00:00:41.200" style="s2">guy. Cincinnati, Ohio. Sweden village.</p>
<p begin="00:00:39.360" end="00:00:43.840" style="s2">It was a great experience. So, I loved</p>
<p begin="00:00:41.200" end="00:00:45.680" style="s2">it. But I&#39;m thrilled to be back in this</p>
<p begin="00:00:43.840" end="00:00:50.480" style="s2">beautiful state which I won all three</p>
<p begin="00:00:45.680" end="00:00:53.640" style="s2">times with the most votes ever gotten.</p>
<p begin="00:00:50.480" end="00:00:53.640" style="s2">Not even</p>
<p begin="00:00:55.199" end="00:01:00.399" style="s2">I even beat Bernie Marino. But John</p>
<p begin="00:00:58.480" end="00:01:03.039" style="s2">Houston&#39;s going to beat me in Vake. I</p>
<p begin="00:01:00.399" end="00:01:04.559" style="s2">hope you beat me, too. I don&#39;t I&#39;m not</p>
<p begin="00:01:03.039" end="00:01:08.199" style="s2">proud.</p>
<p begin="00:01:04.559" end="00:01:08.199" style="s2">I&#39;m not proud.</p>
<p begin="00:01:13.439" end="00:01:20.159" style="s2">&gt;&gt; Boy, oh boy. Since I explained to people</p>
<p begin="00:01:16.799" end="00:01:21.920" style="s2">that he was a phenomenal, not a good a</p>
<p begin="00:01:20.159" end="00:01:24.000" style="s2">phenomenal football player, you have</p>
<p begin="00:01:21.920" end="00:01:26.240" style="s2">really taken on new life. You are</p>
<p begin="00:01:24.000" end="00:01:27.520" style="s2">something.</p>
<p begin="00:01:26.240" end="00:01:29.759" style="s2">You know, I always thought of him as</p>
<p begin="00:01:27.520" end="00:01:32.640" style="s2">this really solid guy. He&#39;s a solid</p>
<p begin="00:01:29.759" end="00:01:34.479" style="s2">rock. But I didn&#39;t see this. And it was</p>
<p begin="00:01:32.640" end="00:01:35.920" style="s2">actually John Gruden, the great coach,</p>
<p begin="00:01:34.479" end="00:01:38.079" style="s2">great coach, and I guess a very good</p>
<p begin="00:01:35.920" end="00:01:39.759" style="s2">quarterback, right? But he was a great</p>
<p begin="00:01:38.079" end="00:01:41.920" style="s2">coach and is a great coach. And he</p>
<p begin="00:01:39.759" end="00:01:44.560" style="s2">explained to me. He said, &quot;No, I&#39;m here</p>
<p begin="00:01:41.920" end="00:01:46.000" style="s2">to see my I&#39;m here to see my teammate.</p>
<p begin="00:01:44.560" end="00:01:47.840" style="s2">Who the hell is your teammate, John?&quot;</p>
<p begin="00:01:46.000" end="00:01:49.439" style="s2">Because I saw him a couple of weeks ago</p>
<p begin="00:01:47.840" end="00:01:51.600" style="s2">at the rally. We had a big rally,</p>
<p begin="00:01:49.439" end="00:01:54.079" style="s2">another one. And I said, &quot;Who&#39;s your</p>
